4 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes what was built. |\n68\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes what was built. |\n69\t\n70\tDeliberate non-edges:\n71\t\n72\t- **E001 ↛ E003**: HLR-3's deliverables (SLO targets, backport policy,\n73\t  supported configuration matrix) are fully specified by the strategy; the\n74\t  assessment's inventory (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error\n75\t  handling) refines the hardening epic, not the support-posture definition.\n76\t  They run in parallel.\n77\t- **E002 ↛ E005**: the Dashboard change is a default/flag flip in a different\n78\t  repo (odh-dashboard); the Dashboard reads the existing\n79\t  LlamaStackDistribution CR and builds against no artifact this strategy\n80\t  produces. Rule 14 parallel. Release-timing coordination (default-on should\n81\t  land with the GA release, not before) is recorded as a risk on the\n82\t  Dashboard epic, not as a DAG edge.\n83\t- **No onboarding epics**: all three components are already in the platform\n84\t  inventory and Konflux-onboarded per architecture context, so no\n85\t  repo/license/konflux onboarding chain is generated (Rule 20 does not apply).\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n88\t\n89\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic |\n90\t|-----|----------|-------------|------|\n91\t| HLR-1 | P0 | A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. | RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 |\n92\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. | RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 |\n93\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Production support posture is in place: documented SLO targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. | RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 |\n94\t| HLR-4 | P1 | Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. | RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 |\n95\t| HLR-5 | P1 | The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). | RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 |\n96\t| HLR-6 | P2 | Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including migration notes from TP. | RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 |\n97\t\n98\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to exactly one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n99\tThe gap-remediation work implied by the problem statement (\"closing the\n100\tquality gaps that TP status currently excuses\") is executed by\n101\tRHAISTRAT-9014-E002 together with HLR-2 — same component, same team, one\n102\tlogical change (GA hardening of the published surface), and its concrete\n103\tscope cannot be known before the assessment resolves, so it cannot be\n104\tscheduled as a standalone epic.\n105\t\n106\t## Health Warnings\n107\t\n108\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n109\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n110\t  and no NFRs. Owner teams were assigned from the architecture-context owning\n111\t  teams (Llama Stack → RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI → TrustyAI, Dashboard → RHOAI\n112\t  Dashboard); the documentation epic is assumed owned by RHOAI GenAI as owner\n113\t  of the primary subject component. Epic acceptance criteria were derived\n114\t  from HLR text.\n115\t- **Planning note (epic size)**: the API stability and GA hardening epic\n116\t  (RHAISTRAT-9014-E002) is above the ~2-week epic-size guideline by the\n117\t  strategy's own admission — the open question states the size of the\n118\t  stability and hardening work is an estimate until the assessment lands.\n119\t  Kept as one epic: the hardening is a single logical change over one\n120\t  published surface by one team, and its concrete scope cannot be enumerated\n121\t  before the assessment resolves, so a pre-emptive split would be arbitrary.\n122\t  **Re-split trigger**: re-split this epic if the assessment's definitive GA\n123\t  scope enumerates remediation items exceeding one sprint of effort or\n124\t  spanning distinct surfaces (e.g. scale-limit test infrastructure vs.\n125\t  API-surface changes) — split along those surface boundaries.\n126\t- **Release coordination (not a DAG edge)**: the Dashboard default-on change\n127\t  should ship with the GA graduation, not expose TP quality to all entitled\n128\t  users early. Recorded as a risk on the Dashboard epic; there is no code\n129\t  artifact dependency.\n130\t- **Priority note**: the documentation epic carries P0 (strategy priority\n131\t  Critical → P0 per the docs-authoring priority exception) even though its\n132\t  HLR is P2 — this is the derivation rule at work, not an inversion.\n133\t\n134\t## Tiered Delivery\n135\t\n136\tNot applicable. The strategy declares no external dependency with uncertain\n137\ttiming (no dependencies table; all components are in-platform and\n138\tKonflux-onboarded per architecture context), so there is no Tier 1 / Tier 2\n139\tsplit.\n140\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ff5dd646c4ed083","agent_id":"ae6dc1172a271c857","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"d25d86c9-2d8c-4e64-ab64-57998efd5f18","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:10:35.384Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e764d327443760c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
