n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Guardrails via TrustyAI function in a GA Llama Stack distribution\n55\t  configuration with no experimental flags enabled.\n56\t- The integration is validated against the versioned, stable Llama Stack API\n57\t  surface and follows its deprecation policy.\n58\t- Automated integration tests cover the guardrails path and pass in CI.\n59\t- The existing Konflux build pipeline for the TrustyAI midstream is green\n60\t  with the completed change set.\n61\t- The technical documentation inputs (supported configuration, usage,\n62\t  limitations) are produced and technically reviewed.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-4 (P1): \"Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n67\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\"\n68\t\n69\t## Risks / Notes\n70\t\n71\t- This epic consumes the stabilized Llama Stack API surface; it is planned\n72\t  after that surface carries its stability guarantee so the supported\n73\t  integration targets the GA API, not the TP-era one.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ff5dd646c4ed083","agent_id":"ae6dc1172a271c857","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"06526198-dce7-43bc-a0bd-b9da1d923977","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:10:42.721Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98637faba9be966e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
