n the published Llama Stack surface (the\n54\t  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the LlamaStackDistribution CRD interfaces).\n55\t- Author and publish the API deprecation policy for the versioned surface.\n56\t- Implement and test the upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases.\n57\t- Remediate the GA-bar gaps that the GA-readiness assessment puts in scope\n58\t  (error handling, scale limits, and other inventoried gaps), per the\n59\t  definitive GA scope.\n60\t- Keep the existing Konflux build pipeline for the Llama Stack midstream\n61\t  green throughout.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- The published API surface is versioned and the versioning is visible to\n66\t  consumers.\n67\t- The API deprecation policy is published and covers the versioned surface.\n68\t- Automated upgrade tests exist and pass for upgrades from each of the last\n69\t  two TP releases.\n70\t- Every gap the GA-readiness assessment placed in the definitive GA scope is\n71\t  remediated in this epic's deliverable or explicitly carried with a recorded\n72\t  deferral decision.\n73\t- No breaking change to the published surface ships undocumented: any\n74\t  unavoidable breaking change follows the new deprecation policy and is\n75\t  covered by the tested upgrade path (rollback/compatibility guarantee).\n76\t- The existing Konflux build pipeline for the Llama Stack midstream is green\n77\t  with the completed change set.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-2 (P0): \"Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n82\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n83\t  two TP releases.\"\n84\t- Additionally executes the gap-remediation scope defined by the\n85\t  GA-readiness assessment (the problem statement's \"closing the quality gaps\n86\t  that TP status currently excuses\").\n87\t\n88\t## Risks / Notes\n89\t\n90\t- Size is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; if the\n91\t  definitive GA scope enumerates remediation beyond one sprint of effort or\n92\t  spanning distinct surfaces, the work should be split along those surface\n93\t  boundaries.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a98f47588918b14e","agent_id":"a7c43dc9dd403e7b9","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"16b01491-6070-4995-bf90-a431daba4ca3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:18:00.258Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81ba4683ad5179aa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
