{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98091c6eee3b74dc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-Readiness Assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's gating unknown: Llama Stack shipped as Tech Preview,\n30\tTP feedback is scattered across support tickets, and no systematic\n31\tGA-readiness assessment has been done. This investigation produces the\n32\tdefinitive GA scope — a consolidated inventory of the gaps between current TP\n33\tquality and the GA bar across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and\n34\terror handling — which the stability and hardening work for the GA graduation\n35\tis planned against.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Consolidate TP feedback from support tickets into a single reviewed backlog\n40\t  of quality signals.\n41\t- Assess the current state of the published API surface: versioning status,\n42\t  breaking changes across TP releases, and undocumented surface.\n43\t- Assess upgrade paths from previous TP releases, including what currently\n44\t  breaks or is untested.\n45\t- Assess scale limits: what is documented, what is measured, and what is\n46\t  unknown.\n47\t- Assess error handling coverage on the published API surface.\n48\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document: a prioritized gap inventory with\n49\t  remediation sizing, stating which gaps are in scope for GA graduation and\n50\t  which are deferred, with rationale.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A GA-readiness report exists that inventories gaps in all four assessed\n55\t  areas (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with\n56\t  each gap traceable to a source (support ticket, code finding, or test\n57\t  result).\n58\t- The report defines the definitive GA scope: an explicit in-scope vs.\n59\t  deferred decision per gap, with rationale.\n60\t- The support-ticket feedback corpus has been reviewed end to end, so no\n61\t  known TP feedback source is left out of the inventory.\n62\t- The report is delivered to the strategy stakeholders for GA scope sign-off.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n67\t  current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n68\t  error handling), producing the definitive GA scope.\" This epic is that\n69\t  assessment.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- Scale-limit verification may require a live cluster or performance\n74\t  environment; desk analysis of code, tests, and tickets covers the rest.\n75\t- The final GA-scope sign-off is a stakeholder decision informed by this\n76\t  investigation's technical inventory.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de9ef08aa817306","agent_id":"a3f3f864f5c7bc769","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"fb027ed1-9067-4ed1-ae07-20c9f881c095","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:20:04.902Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98091c6eee3b74dc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
