{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a86ead07e0735ef9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# TrustyAI Guardrails as a Supported Llama Stack Integration\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tPromotes safety guardrails via TrustyAI for Llama Stack from an experimental\n35\tflag to a supported, documented integration for GA distributions: hardened,\n36\ttested against the stabilized Llama Stack API surface, and usable without\n37\texperimental opt-in.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Harden the TrustyAI guardrails integration to support standards: error\n42\t  handling, configuration validation, and compatibility with the versioned\n43\t  Llama Stack API surface and its deprecation policy.\n44\t- Remove the experimental-flag gating so the integration is a supported\n45\t  configuration in GA Llama Stack distributions.\n46\t- Validate guardrails enforcement end to end through the Llama Stack safety /\n47\t  provider-plugin surface with TrustyAI as the guardrails provider.\n48\t- Add integration-level automated tests running in CI.\n49\t- Produce the technically reviewed technical documentation inputs — supported\n50\t  configuration, usage, and known limitations — as SME input handed off to the\n51\t  GA documentation uplift work; this epic does not author or publish the\n52\t  end-user documentation itself.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Guardrails via TrustyAI function in a GA Llama Stack distribution\n57\t  configuration with no experimental flags enabled.\n58\t- The integration is validated against the versioned, stable Llama Stack API\n59\t  surface and follows its deprecation policy.\n60\t- Automated integration tests cover the guardrails path and pass in CI.\n61\t- The existing Konflux build pipeline for the TrustyAI midstream is green\n62\t  with the completed change set.\n63\t- The technical documentation inputs (supported configuration, usage,\n64\t  limitations) are produced, technically reviewed, and handed off to the GA\n65\t  documentation uplift work as SME input — they are not a standalone\n66\t  documentation deliverable of this epic.\n67\t- Guardrails failure behavior in a supported configuration (no experimental\n68\t  flags) is defined and tested: when the TrustyAI guardrails provider is\n69\t  unavailable or misconfigured, the failure mode is defined and covered by the\n70\t  automated integration tests.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-4 (P1): \"Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n75\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\"\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- This epic consumes the stabilized Llama Stack API surface; it is planned\n80\t  after that surface carries its stability guarantee so the supported\n81\t  integration targets the GA API, not the TP-era one.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de9ef08aa817306","agent_id":"a3f3f864f5c7bc769","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"f1b9a21a-8d1c-48d6-8b5f-6e2b07455cfa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:20:08.882Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a86ead07e0735ef9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]