{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93f92c57061520b2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: Dashboard Llama Stack management default-on for entitled clusters\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 9\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard Llama Stack Management Default-On for Entitled Clusters\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRemoves the Tech Preview opt-in gate for Llama Stack management in the\n34\tDashboard: on entitled clusters, Llama Stack management is enabled by\n35\tdefault, with no opt-in required.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Change the Dashboard enablement logic for Llama Stack management from\n40\t  opt-in to default-on for entitled clusters.\n41\t- Handle the entitlement check so clusters without entitlement keep their\n42\t  current behavior.\n43\t- Preserve a rollback path: enablement remains controllable through the\n44\t  existing per-component Dashboard configuration (feature flags / defaults),\n45\t  so the default-on can be reverted without a code rollback.\n46\t- Update Dashboard tests covering the default-on, entitled, and\n47\t  non-entitled paths.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- On an entitled cluster with default Dashboard configuration, Llama Stack\n52\t  management surfaces without any opt-in action.\n53\t- On a cluster without entitlement, Dashboard behavior is unchanged from\n54\t  before this change.\n55\t- The enablement default is reversible through the existing Dashboard\n56\t  configuration mechanism (rollback path verified).\n57\t- Dashboard test suites pass, including new coverage for the default-on and\n58\t  non-entitled paths.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-5 (P1): \"The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n63\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\"\n64\t\n65\t## Risks / Notes\n66\t\n67\t- Release coordination: the default-on flip should ship with the Llama Stack\n68\t  GA graduation so TP-quality experience is not exposed by default to all\n69\t  entitled users early. This is a release-timing coordination risk, not a\n70\t  code dependency — the Dashboard change itself touches only Dashboard\n71\t  configuration and enablement logic.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de9ef08aa817306","agent_id":"a3f3f864f5c7bc769","session_id":"0204fee7-ce49-4572-ac85-f81f526b0c75","uuid":"3fcf7c5f-b1f3-40c5-915a-8c1bf4439ba8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:20:10.971Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93f92c57061520b2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
